  "Objects are Analog, Binary and Multi-state Values only. Rows without a read-only mark in the manual are listed as writable.",
  "Objects that show psi, °C and °F use the unit selected by INMODE.",
  "Start-up settings can be read but not written over BACnet; Heat-Timer says to set them at the panel first.",
  "The manual prints some rows as ranges (BTIME00-19 = 0-19; FIRE00-19 = 200-219; LOCK00-19 = 900-919; MAN00-19 = 1100-1119; MODE00-19 = 1400-1419; MODST00-19 = 1500-1519; MTRIM00-19 = 1600-1619; STONOFF00-19 = 2900-2919; STPCT00-19 = 3000-3019). Only the first and last printed objects of each range are listed here; the ones in between follow the same pattern.",
  "Per-stage objects come in blocks of 20 (00-19).",
  "Variable list: manual pages 16-17."
 ],
